% COORDINATION_FUNCTION: Provides a unified, historically continuous ethical vocabulary (dignity, subsidiarity, common good, solidarity) that Catholic institutions, and some secular actors seeking moral grounding, can use to evaluate and resist AI applications perceived as dehumanizing — filling a real gap where purely procedural or market-based governance frameworks offer no substantive anthropology to adjudicate hard cases (lethal autonomous weapons, simulated companionship, predictive policing).
% TRANSFER_FUNCTION: Moves moral authority and institutional legitimacy toward the Magisterium and Catholic-affiliated universities, hospitals, and NGOs (who gain funding, convening power, and policy access), and moves reputational and compliance costs onto AI developers and researchers whose projects conflict with Catholic anthropology — particularly transhumanist and certain surveillance/autonomous-weapons programs. No direct monetary transfer occurs; the currency is legitimacy, access, and moral standing.
% ABSENT_VOICES: Non-Catholic theological traditions with independently developed personhood doctrines are largely absent from the drafting process, despite the doctrine claiming to speak for human dignity universally. Transhumanist researchers and technocratic developers are named as targets but are not invited co-authors of the anthropology that constrains them. Vulnerable populations, workers, and families — the named beneficiaries — are represented by advocacy rather than direct participation.
% DISAPPEARANCE_RATIONALE: From the Magisterium's own account, disappearance would leave AI governance to secular and market logics it regards as insufficiently protective of the person, producing real harm to vulnerable groups (world_rearranges). From a technocratic developer's account, disappearance would simply remove one non-binding moral voice among many competing frameworks that already coexist in a pluralist governance landscape, changing little in actual regulatory outcomes (world_unchanged). The verdict depends on how much causal weight one assigns to moral suasion absent binding legal force.
